// The game's copy helpers and its table lookup pass the borrow check: a copy of a local
// buffer's bytes is independent of the buffer, and a lookup's result doesn't borrow its key.
// The helpers are `copy_bytes` and `copy_lower` of kotor/lib/engine/object.ctx as they are
// today, cut out of it by cut.ctx into copies.ctx; kotor-probe.ctx calls them, and
// `twoda::get_string`, with locals.
//# build cut: cut.ctx
//# $ {cut} {repo}/kotor/lib/engine/object.ctx copies.ctx copy_bytes copy_lower
//# stdout:
//| fn copy_bytes: {n} bytes
//| fn copy_lower: {n} bytes
//# file copies.ctx has:
//| namespace object {
//|     fn copy_bytes {any}
//# file copies.ctx has:
//|     }
//|     fn copy_lower {any}

// The program builds: ctxc gives its C without an error, and the
// C compiles and links. It isn't run: its `main` is empty.
//# $ ctxc build probe.c {std} -- {repo}/kotor/lib/base/ci.ctx {repo}/kotor/lib/base/le.ctx {repo}/kotor/lib/base/text.ctx {repo}/kotor/lib/formats/twoda.ctx copies.ctx kotor-probe.ctx
//# exit: 0
//# $ cc {cflags} -I {home}/ctxc/rt probe.c {home}/ctxc/rt/ctxrt.c -lm -o probe{exe} {stack}
//# exit: 0
//# exists probe{exe}
